WEBVTT

01:49.526 --> 01:56.533
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE

02:01.454 --> 02:06.251
1 YEAR AGO
ONGSEONG HOSPITAL, GYEONGSEONG

02:11.256 --> 02:14.884
Ryu Sachimoto, graduated
from Tokyo University of the Arts…

02:15.885 --> 02:17.095
You volunteered?

02:17.178 --> 02:18.179
Yes.

02:18.680 --> 02:21.766
To serve His Majesty
and the Empire of Japan--

02:21.850 --> 02:24.352
And get paid well while you're at it.

02:33.153 --> 02:34.988
What is this, sir?

02:35.071 --> 02:36.656
It's called Kaitai Shinsho.

02:38.116 --> 02:40.118
You mean a book on anatomy?

02:41.953 --> 02:46.666
Books such as those have been around
in Germany since 1722.

02:46.749 --> 02:48.585
Although lagging behind,

02:48.668 --> 02:51.921
we're working to elevate
our empire's medical standards

02:52.005 --> 02:57.343
here at Ongseong Hospital via a vast range
of research studies and experiments.

02:58.261 --> 03:00.889
Your job is to keep a record of them.

03:01.472 --> 03:02.599
So,

03:03.308 --> 03:05.643
what I'm supposed to draw is…

03:11.524 --> 03:14.569
Now, which part shall we work on today?

03:16.696 --> 03:18.990
We have a new painter with us today.

03:19.073 --> 03:21.826
Why don't we start off lightly
by opening up the abdomen?

03:22.493 --> 03:23.328
Yes, sir.

03:24.704 --> 03:25.538
Scalpel.

03:27.040 --> 03:28.291
Please don't kill me.

03:28.374 --> 03:31.002
Please. Please spare me!

03:31.836 --> 03:33.379
Doctor! Please!

03:33.463 --> 03:35.131
Please don't kill me!

03:48.519 --> 03:51.022
Sachimoto!

03:51.606 --> 03:53.107
Get back here at once!

03:53.650 --> 03:57.654
- I was merely a penniless painter.
- Sachimoto!

03:58.905 --> 04:00.406
I needed money,

04:01.032 --> 04:04.244
and I chose Joseon
because of the high pay, but…

04:27.308 --> 04:28.643
There's no need to cry.

04:31.229 --> 04:35.858
You'll get used to it soon enough,
just like everyone else here.

04:37.193 --> 04:39.821
That's the thing about humans.

04:39.904 --> 04:43.825
We are quick to adapt to anything.

04:44.909 --> 04:46.411
Whether it be longing…

04:49.789 --> 04:51.457
or anguish.

04:55.586 --> 04:58.047
Hey, time's up. Hurry up.

07:16.519 --> 07:20.022
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE
BETWEEN LONGING AND ANGUISH

07:20.106 --> 07:22.483
EPISODE 2
MOTHER

07:48.593 --> 07:51.262
Why have you accepted
such a man's request?

07:51.846 --> 07:53.848
Well, there was no reason not to.

07:54.474 --> 07:58.728
That man will find the missing person.
We will obtain information on Sachimoto.

07:58.811 --> 08:00.938
He is an insolent and shameless man.

08:02.315 --> 08:04.317
Don't be so quick to judge a person.

08:05.234 --> 08:06.861
I can tell by the way he speaks,

08:08.279 --> 08:10.907
and how he treats
others' problems so lightly.

08:10.990 --> 08:14.076
We are nothing but mere sleuths to him.

08:16.537 --> 08:18.080
We've reached an agreement.

08:18.164 --> 08:20.666
All we need to do
is work toward our mutual benefit.

08:22.835 --> 08:23.878
This case…

08:25.963 --> 08:27.632
I have a bad feeling about it.

08:29.550 --> 08:31.802
I had the same feeling on Manwol Island,

08:33.179 --> 08:35.014
and you were badly hurt then.

08:38.684 --> 08:40.811
This will be the last time, Chae-ok.

08:43.773 --> 08:45.107
After this is over,

08:46.108 --> 08:47.527
you should return home.

08:48.110 --> 08:49.362
What about Mother?

08:51.489 --> 08:54.700
Finding your mother is my fate
and my burden to bear.

08:56.494 --> 08:59.288
I can't let you bear it any longer.

08:59.372 --> 09:00.248
Father.

09:00.331 --> 09:02.875
You should live your own life.

09:04.335 --> 09:06.254
This is our last job together.

09:29.277 --> 09:32.405
Until the cherry blossoms fall.

09:52.133 --> 09:55.094
What do you think about those sleuths?

09:56.262 --> 09:58.014
Do you think they have what it takes?

09:58.681 --> 10:00.266
Judging by what they said,

10:01.726 --> 10:03.728
they didn't strike me as amateurs.

10:44.560 --> 10:46.228
Who's taking the next shift?

10:46.312 --> 10:47.897
I heard it was Kinoshita.

10:47.980 --> 10:50.399
Oh, the new kid?

10:50.483 --> 10:51.651
He's no good.

12:07.351 --> 12:08.644
- Let's go.
- Yes, sir!

13:16.629 --> 13:19.840
How is it
that we can't find a single lead?

13:19.924 --> 13:22.551
I combed through
Myeong-ja's favorite tea shops,

13:22.635 --> 13:26.388
restaurants, boutiques, and shoe stores.
No one knows her whereabouts.

13:26.472 --> 13:27.973
How is this possible?

13:28.474 --> 13:31.769
I even visited
that rickshaw office she frequents,

13:31.852 --> 13:33.187
but even they didn't know.

13:33.270 --> 13:35.606
No one's given her a ride or seen her.

13:35.689 --> 13:37.900
Gosh, is she gone with the wind?

13:37.983 --> 13:39.902
She disappeared without a trace.

13:39.985 --> 13:43.280
It's as if she evaporated. That's it.
Myeong-ja evaporated.

13:44.406 --> 13:47.952
A person always leaves behind
some trace wherever they go.

13:48.035 --> 13:49.453
We just haven't found it.

13:52.706 --> 13:57.044
By the way, is that really
how they're tailing us right now?

13:57.127 --> 13:58.796
Do they think we're idiots?

13:58.879 --> 14:02.132
I mean, that's the most conspicuous tail
I have ever seen.

14:02.800 --> 14:06.470
It's quite unsettling to pretend
to not notice them. Sheesh!

14:08.556 --> 14:11.642
- Fighting over that chamber pot.
- Has he lost his mind?

14:14.728 --> 14:18.816
Answer me!
What color does this look like to you?

14:19.400 --> 14:20.317
Well…

14:21.026 --> 14:22.278
It's white.

14:22.361 --> 14:25.990
And what do you call
white porcelain in Joseon?

14:26.574 --> 14:27.992
Baekja, sir.

14:29.493 --> 14:30.619
Then…

14:32.663 --> 14:33.581
what is this?

14:35.124 --> 14:36.458
Answer me!

14:36.542 --> 14:38.377
I'm asking you what this is!

14:41.171 --> 14:42.172
Let's see.

14:43.299 --> 14:45.009
How do I put this?

14:45.092 --> 14:47.720
It's too shoddy
to be called fine porcelain.

14:47.803 --> 14:50.931
It looks like
an ordinary piece of pottery to me.

14:51.015 --> 14:53.893
And yet, I paid 100 won for that.

14:54.727 --> 14:55.561
So what?

14:56.145 --> 15:00.024
How much would you give me
if I were to pawn it here?

15:00.107 --> 15:02.067
Do you have a written guarantee on you?

15:02.610 --> 15:04.361
A receipt would also be fine.

15:07.740 --> 15:08.908
I don't have either.

15:13.245 --> 15:16.832
You shelled out 100 won for a chamber pot
that's barely worth 10 jeon,

15:17.333 --> 15:19.084
and you don't have a guarantee
or a receipt?

15:19.710 --> 15:23.464
It's clear to me that you were scammed.

15:23.547 --> 15:28.052
This is a matter for the police bureau,
not a pawnshop.

15:31.639 --> 15:32.473
Master Jang.

15:33.891 --> 15:36.060
Be a good man and just take the pot.

15:36.644 --> 15:39.939
I heard Ishikawa will be confiscating
everything you own.

15:40.773 --> 15:41.774
Says who?

15:41.857 --> 15:45.027
Everyone in Bonjeong
knows about it already.

15:45.110 --> 15:47.613
The House of Golden Treasure
will have a new master.

15:48.739 --> 15:53.202
You're going to lose everything anyway.
What's one more chamber pot to you?

15:57.039 --> 15:58.832
Would you look at this bastard?

15:59.583 --> 16:01.001
What are you yapping about?

16:01.085 --> 16:02.086
What?

16:02.753 --> 16:03.837
"This bastard"?

16:03.921 --> 16:06.423
Stop disrupting my business and get out.

16:06.507 --> 16:08.634
Keep pushing your luck
and you might get hurt.

16:08.717 --> 16:11.512
Oh, and try not to speak
the Joseon tongue if you can.

16:11.595 --> 16:13.514
Your pronunciation sucks.

16:13.597 --> 16:14.431
It's the worst!

16:15.182 --> 16:16.558
Damn you!

16:17.101 --> 16:18.477
You're dead!

16:35.911 --> 16:39.498
The House of Golden Treasure
is owned by me, Jang Tae-sang,

16:39.581 --> 16:41.750
and it will stay that way.

16:42.334 --> 16:47.423
So if you cause a disturbance in my shop
or even dare to dream of robbing me,

16:47.506 --> 16:49.633
you better be prepared

16:49.717 --> 16:52.344
to either die or come very close to dying.

16:55.597 --> 16:57.725
Come on! My arm's hurting!

16:58.642 --> 17:01.729
My arm keeps giving out.
It must be my age.

17:01.812 --> 17:04.023
See? Look…

17:04.857 --> 17:05.858
Hey.

17:07.276 --> 17:08.360
You should leave.

17:16.577 --> 17:18.203
- Move!
- Get lost!

17:18.287 --> 17:19.455
Out of the way!

17:25.044 --> 17:26.003
Let's go.

17:34.678 --> 17:36.680
From now on, we must all stay vigilant.

17:37.598 --> 17:38.515
What?

17:39.975 --> 17:41.310
What do you mean?

17:41.393 --> 17:43.479
He means we should find Myeong-ja soon,

17:43.562 --> 17:47.316
or else scoundrels like him
will keep showing up to bother us.

17:48.901 --> 17:50.152
Which reminds me.

17:54.364 --> 17:56.700
They found the last place
Myeong-ja visited.

17:57.785 --> 17:58.619
What?

18:08.170 --> 18:11.715
We found the rickshaw puller
who gave her a ride seven days ago.

18:13.050 --> 18:15.636
What? No way! That can't be!

18:15.719 --> 18:19.264
I chased down every single puller
working for Spring Moon Hall.

18:19.348 --> 18:22.476
I asked around
and investigated everything myself!

18:22.976 --> 18:24.895
The man doesn't work for Spring Moon Hall.

18:27.523 --> 18:28.398
Then what?

18:28.482 --> 18:30.192
You said she could've been killed.

18:31.819 --> 18:33.987
So we thought about
who could've killed her,

18:34.655 --> 18:36.365
and only one person came to mind.

18:54.967 --> 18:56.009
Where's Mr. Takashi?

18:56.593 --> 18:59.680
He fell ill and will rest
for three to four days.

19:02.975 --> 19:04.226
Lady Yukiko Maeda.

19:07.271 --> 19:09.857
So Yukiko Maeda called Myeong-ja out?

19:09.940 --> 19:12.776
She was called
to Ishikawa's house at first,

19:12.860 --> 19:15.362
then moved elsewhere shortly after.

19:16.280 --> 19:17.364
Where would that be?

19:17.948 --> 19:19.116
Ongseong Hospital.

19:19.908 --> 19:22.035
Ong… Ongseong Hospital?

19:22.870 --> 19:23.954
Are you certain?

19:32.838 --> 19:34.548
Please don't kill me!

19:35.465 --> 19:38.177
You are certain it was Ongseong Hospital?

19:38.260 --> 19:41.889
Yes! I swear it was Ongseong Hospital!

19:41.972 --> 19:45.392
I swear it on my mother
and father's lives!

19:45.475 --> 19:46.977
It was Ongseong Hospital!

19:47.060 --> 19:51.273
I told you, I took her there myself!

19:53.233 --> 19:57.279
She disappeared after the puller
dropped her off at Ongseong Hospital,

19:57.863 --> 20:01.450
so it is likely that she's still in there,
don't you think?

20:01.533 --> 20:04.119
Gosh, no. That makes no sense.

20:04.203 --> 20:05.746
What doesn't make sense?

20:05.829 --> 20:09.249
Look, here's the thing
about Ongseong Hospital.

20:09.333 --> 20:10.626
It's hard to get in there

20:10.709 --> 20:15.422
unless you are Japanese military, police,
or a Government-General official.

20:15.505 --> 20:17.925
A Joseon courtesan
could never get past its gates!

20:18.008 --> 20:22.054
You don't know how tight their security is
at the gate with all the inspections.

20:23.263 --> 20:27.100
What if Yukiko Maeda pulled some strings
and arranged it?

20:27.184 --> 20:28.602
Why would she do that?

20:29.228 --> 20:33.273
Why would she take her husband's mistress
to a Japanese-only hospital?

20:33.357 --> 20:35.734
We can get inside the hospital
to figure that out.

20:35.817 --> 20:38.153
My God, what is the matter with you?

20:38.237 --> 20:41.323
I just said that we Joseon-borns
are not allowed in there!

20:41.406 --> 20:43.659
I heard that Master Jang
has good connections.

20:45.953 --> 20:47.829
But not good enough to get us inside?

20:52.417 --> 20:56.463
Well, I do know some Joseon individuals
who can visit that hospital.

20:56.546 --> 20:58.548
So, can we get in or not?

20:58.632 --> 21:00.300
That I'll have to see.

21:00.384 --> 21:03.804
Forget it. If you can't make it happen,
we'll find a way.

21:03.887 --> 21:07.224
You're an impatient one, aren't you?
Who says I can't do it?

21:07.307 --> 21:09.810
I'm just saying, let's make a plan.

21:09.893 --> 21:13.563
We ought to be fully prepared
in whatever we do.

21:13.647 --> 21:14.898
Don't you know that?

21:24.283 --> 21:25.909
Something on my face?

21:38.005 --> 21:39.006
What are you doing?

21:39.631 --> 21:41.758
Oh. Give these to the two outside.

21:41.842 --> 21:43.176
What's your plan?

21:43.260 --> 21:44.803
How dare they doubt me?

21:45.304 --> 21:49.349
I'll show them
how shrewd and meticulous I am.

21:49.433 --> 21:51.601
What's the money for?
What are you up to this time?

21:52.269 --> 21:53.353
What do you think?

21:53.937 --> 21:56.857
Doing the impossible, of course.

22:04.990 --> 22:06.491
- What is this?
- Money.

22:07.784 --> 22:08.618
It's money.

22:09.453 --> 22:12.289
I don't care if you use it
for the independence movement.

22:12.372 --> 22:15.083
I'm giving it to you,
so spend it as you wish.

22:17.669 --> 22:19.087
What trick are you pulling?

22:23.842 --> 22:25.093
Let me borrow your ID.

22:25.177 --> 22:26.470
My ID?

22:26.553 --> 22:30.223
Only a few Joseon people in Gyeongseong
are allowed into Ongseong Hospital,

22:30.724 --> 22:32.726
and your family is among them.

22:33.352 --> 22:34.811
- Am I right?
- Why do you ask?

22:35.729 --> 22:36.730
Are you unwell?

22:37.314 --> 22:38.482
No, not me.

22:38.565 --> 22:39.483
Wait!

22:40.150 --> 22:43.904
If this has anything to do with Ishikawa,
leave me out of it.

22:47.240 --> 22:50.827
Think of it as saving your friend's life.

22:50.911 --> 22:53.580
If you still consider me a friend,
that is.

22:53.663 --> 22:55.665
If you're not ill, then who is?

22:56.458 --> 22:59.044
I should at least know who it is
before I lend it to you.

22:59.127 --> 23:01.922
Don't ask too many questions.
It's for your own good.

23:02.005 --> 23:05.801
You're here to steal my identity,
and you're worried about me?

23:07.052 --> 23:07.886
Will you help?

23:10.722 --> 23:13.809
How wonderful it would be
for you to use such passion for us.

23:18.146 --> 23:23.026
Sorry, but I don't daydream
about something like independence.

23:23.944 --> 23:27.364
How can I dare to take back
what even the king failed to protect?

23:28.156 --> 23:30.492
All I want, in these turbulent times,

23:31.076 --> 23:33.120
is to strive as stubbornly as I can

23:33.870 --> 23:36.706
to stay alive and safe day after day.

23:37.707 --> 23:38.667
So,

23:40.544 --> 23:41.795
will you do this for me?

23:48.427 --> 23:49.719
Return it in one piece.

23:53.140 --> 23:54.057
Will do.

24:08.071 --> 24:09.156
So, how did it go?

24:10.824 --> 24:12.617
Are the sleuths here yet?

24:15.245 --> 24:16.496
Oh, there they are.

24:16.997 --> 24:19.291
That one's pretty too!

24:21.251 --> 24:22.169
So beautiful!

24:56.953 --> 24:58.955
- Let's get going.
- Huh?

24:59.748 --> 25:00.874
We don't have all day.

25:01.500 --> 25:03.418
Yes, we should go.

25:03.502 --> 25:04.503
Please hop in.

25:13.094 --> 25:16.598
Oh, it's good manners
to help a lady get in the car.

25:17.849 --> 25:18.850
No need.

25:31.154 --> 25:32.364
Let's go.

25:57.097 --> 25:57.931
Identification.

26:00.976 --> 26:02.727
This is my master.

26:02.811 --> 26:05.188
You're familiar
with the Bugang Company, aren't you?

26:05.272 --> 26:07.065
He's the firstborn son of the family.

26:11.945 --> 26:13.446
Are they with you?

26:15.574 --> 26:19.953
They are my master's fiancée
and her father.

26:25.417 --> 26:29.004
Oh, it's almost time for our appointment.

26:30.338 --> 26:31.423
Please hurry.

26:31.506 --> 26:36.219
Dr. Takahashi absolutely hates it
when people are late for appointments.

26:37.429 --> 26:39.014
Damn Josenjing…

26:40.265 --> 26:41.516
Hey, let them through!

26:41.600 --> 26:42.851
Thank you!

26:48.523 --> 26:49.441
Wait, hold up!

27:06.875 --> 27:07.959
You forgot this.

27:08.043 --> 27:10.086
Oh, silly me! Anyway…

27:10.170 --> 27:11.338
Thank you, sir!

27:44.871 --> 27:45.789
Ongseong Hospital?

27:45.872 --> 27:49.626
Yes, sir.
He just went in with some company.

27:50.377 --> 27:53.713
Should I tell him to stay and keep watch?

28:18.321 --> 28:20.573
RECORDS ROOM

28:41.136 --> 28:43.179
I'm here to see Dr. Takahashi.

28:44.264 --> 28:45.515
Dr. Takahashi?

28:46.766 --> 28:49.018
Dr. Takahashi is our family physician.

28:49.102 --> 28:51.062
But he will be out of the office today.

28:51.146 --> 28:53.940
He plays soft tennis
every Thursday afternoon.

28:55.358 --> 28:56.443
Even better.

28:56.526 --> 28:59.279
Dr. Takahashi is out of the office
this afternoon.

28:59.362 --> 29:02.490
But I made an appointment
to see him today.

29:03.283 --> 29:05.285
Could you check one more time?

29:06.161 --> 29:08.163
- Please wait a moment.
- Sure.

29:25.805 --> 29:26.848
Oh, my stomach!

29:27.766 --> 29:28.600
What's wrong?

29:32.270 --> 29:33.229
Are you all right?

29:33.813 --> 29:35.690
- Where does it hurt?
- My stomach!

29:35.774 --> 29:36.900
Hey, Gap-pyeong!

29:37.692 --> 29:38.526
Gap-pyeong!

29:39.402 --> 29:41.488
- Are you all right?
- Gap-pyeong!

29:41.571 --> 29:45.074
- It's coming out of my bottom!
- What's coming out of your bottom?

29:45.158 --> 29:46.659
Oh, it hurts!

29:46.743 --> 29:48.077
What's coming out?

29:48.161 --> 29:49.662
- It's coming out!
- Is it?

29:56.753 --> 29:57.587
Hang in there!

29:57.670 --> 29:59.422
Are there any doctors? A doctor!

30:00.173 --> 30:01.007
Doctor!

30:05.762 --> 30:06.763
Hang in there!

30:11.976 --> 30:13.520
Akiko…

30:14.312 --> 30:15.563
Akiko…

30:21.110 --> 30:22.403
Akiko…

30:32.247 --> 30:33.248
Who are you?

30:40.129 --> 30:41.798
What are you doing here?

30:43.925 --> 30:44.843
I…

30:46.636 --> 30:48.221
got a bit lost.

30:48.304 --> 30:52.183
If you got lost,
why were you flipping through the records?

30:53.017 --> 30:55.728
A friend of mine
is staying at this hospital,

30:56.437 --> 30:58.189
but I just can't seem to find them.

31:04.487 --> 31:06.072
I can tell you're from Joseon.

31:06.698 --> 31:08.366
Let's not make a scene.

31:08.449 --> 31:10.368
I'll leave quietly.

31:13.580 --> 31:14.414
Is that all right?

31:14.998 --> 31:15.999
Why are you here?

31:16.958 --> 31:18.293
Reveal who you are first.

31:25.758 --> 31:27.927
Don't make a scene, she said.

31:33.474 --> 31:36.519
Are you… from Manchuria?

31:38.146 --> 31:39.480
Who are you?

31:46.529 --> 31:49.490
The doctor will be here soon.
Hang in there.

31:49.574 --> 31:52.076
I think the doctor's here. He's here!

31:56.331 --> 31:58.333
This should ease his pain for now.

32:01.085 --> 32:02.837
- Take off his jacket!
- Yes, Doctor.

32:02.921 --> 32:04.339
Wait, no!

32:04.422 --> 32:05.673
No…

32:05.757 --> 32:07.216
No, stop!

32:07.300 --> 32:08.384
You can't!

32:09.093 --> 32:11.137
Please don't kill me! Please!

32:11.638 --> 32:13.389
Master, please!

32:14.766 --> 32:16.351
Please, Master…

32:16.434 --> 32:18.019
- Let's hurry!
- Yes, Doctor!

32:18.102 --> 32:19.771
It's okay. You'll feel better soon.

32:19.854 --> 32:21.147
No!

32:21.230 --> 32:22.482
- Gap-pyeong!
- No…

32:22.565 --> 32:24.400
Hey, you! Come here!

32:25.068 --> 32:26.653
Let's not do this!

32:29.030 --> 32:30.531
Come here!

32:32.033 --> 32:35.620
Oh, hold on! Hold on a second…

32:41.751 --> 32:43.753
- What?
- The pain's suddenly gone.

32:43.836 --> 32:44.754
Really?

32:46.464 --> 32:48.800
How can this be?
My pain is completely gone!

32:48.883 --> 32:50.051
What was that?

32:50.134 --> 32:52.387
It doesn't hurt anymore, Doctor!

32:52.470 --> 32:53.888
That's amazing!

32:55.682 --> 32:58.726
Thank you, sir.
You truly are a skilled doctor!

33:08.861 --> 33:09.779
Fascinating.

33:13.032 --> 33:15.576
Were you going to let them
give me that shot?

33:16.369 --> 33:17.578
Well, they didn't.

33:21.708 --> 33:22.625
What was that?

33:23.584 --> 33:25.545
What's going on? Did you hear that?

33:25.628 --> 33:26.838
Please don't be alarmed!

33:26.921 --> 33:30.216
The nearby military base
must be holding another target practice.

33:32.010 --> 33:35.263
That's strange. The sound came
from underneath the building.

33:35.346 --> 33:36.764
Let's move for now.

33:37.348 --> 33:38.266
Follow me.

33:46.607 --> 33:48.693
- Why did you open fire?
- We failed to capture it.

33:49.277 --> 33:51.529
Two were attacked
before we approached the door!

33:52.030 --> 33:54.615
One corporal is still alive, sir!

33:55.199 --> 33:56.367
Please help me!

33:57.160 --> 33:58.286
Please help…

34:03.916 --> 34:04.751
What should we do?

34:12.383 --> 34:14.510
I'll go and rescue the corporal!

34:14.594 --> 34:16.804
Stay still. Nobody move!

34:16.888 --> 34:18.639
Please let me save him, sir!

34:19.807 --> 34:20.808
Be quiet.

34:20.892 --> 34:22.727
Don't move a muscle!

34:23.686 --> 34:26.939
This experiment is
of vital importance to us.

34:27.023 --> 34:27.857
Understood?

34:29.525 --> 34:32.070
Colonel Kato. Over there.

34:33.571 --> 34:35.990
What… is that thing?

34:36.074 --> 34:37.408
Save me!

34:38.493 --> 34:39.368
Please…

34:41.829 --> 34:43.122
Please save me!

34:44.457 --> 34:45.666
Help me!

34:45.750 --> 34:46.918
Please…

35:12.068 --> 35:13.319
Stop it!

35:13.402 --> 35:14.946
No! Stop right there!

35:37.969 --> 35:39.011
She is a goddess.

35:46.060 --> 35:47.770
A goddess has been born!

36:24.724 --> 36:26.684
Hey, what are you doing here?

36:27.185 --> 36:28.394
What is going on?

36:28.477 --> 36:30.980
We will be spending the night here.

36:31.063 --> 36:32.273
What?

36:32.356 --> 36:34.400
What about us? Us too?

36:34.483 --> 36:37.737
You will only get in the way,
so I suggest you get out.

36:38.654 --> 36:41.032
At least tell us what's going on.

36:44.410 --> 36:46.370
There is a military ward in the back.

36:47.163 --> 36:49.415
Something very fishy is going on
in the basement.

36:49.916 --> 36:53.502
They say Joseon people
from Seodaemun Prison are sent there,

36:54.337 --> 36:56.088
but apparently, none of them

36:57.131 --> 36:58.633
have come back.

37:01.260 --> 37:02.762
Is Myeong-ja in there too?

37:03.387 --> 37:05.139
We're planning to find that out.

37:05.223 --> 37:06.224
What…

37:07.642 --> 37:09.977
Where did you even get that information?

37:15.524 --> 37:17.944
Something's afoot
in the military ward right now.

37:18.027 --> 37:19.862
Why don't you come back another day?

37:20.738 --> 37:22.406
We don't have time for that.

37:22.490 --> 37:25.076
Just lead the way.
We'll take care of the rest.

37:33.709 --> 37:34.710
Wait, just…

37:38.798 --> 37:40.049
Just…

37:40.132 --> 37:42.218
Just what is going on right now?

37:42.301 --> 37:45.763
What could this janitor
possibly have told you that's--

37:45.846 --> 37:50.059
My younger brother was transferred here
from Seodaemun Prison a year ago.

37:51.477 --> 37:55.314
He was moved here because of a high fever,
but I've lost contact with him ever since.

37:55.815 --> 37:58.734
I've looked for him,
but he wasn't even on the records here.

37:58.818 --> 38:01.821
Oh dear. So you snuck in here to find him.

38:02.446 --> 38:05.950
Why should we believe you?
You're a complete stranger.

38:15.960 --> 38:16.794
What's that?

38:16.877 --> 38:19.088
It's the sign of the Patriotic Society.

38:20.298 --> 38:22.425
Heck, it's one of the independence groups.

38:25.177 --> 38:26.679
You should head back first.

38:27.555 --> 38:31.142
We'll check if Myeong-ja is actually here
and send you a message.

38:32.643 --> 38:33.477
But…

38:33.561 --> 38:34.895
I'm ready.

38:35.479 --> 38:36.397
Follow me.

38:38.149 --> 38:39.066
Hey, wait.

38:39.150 --> 38:41.652
Oh, yeah. Thank you for the clothes.

38:41.736 --> 38:43.988
You know that's not what I meant.

38:47.992 --> 38:50.244
Did you have something else to say?

38:52.788 --> 38:53.706
What is it?

38:54.999 --> 38:55.833
Say it.

39:01.130 --> 39:01.964
Well,

39:03.257 --> 39:04.842
I just…

39:07.553 --> 39:10.598
I just think this plan is too reckless,
so I'm saying

39:12.224 --> 39:15.186
we should come up with a safer plan.

39:15.269 --> 39:17.063
"Until the cherry blossoms fall."

39:18.606 --> 39:22.276
Once cherry blossoms open,
they reach full bloom quickly.

39:22.360 --> 39:25.571
Then they begin to fall
just when you think they've all bloomed.

39:26.280 --> 39:28.783
So we have no time or reason to delay.

39:28.866 --> 39:31.952
Still, it wasn't part of the plan
for you to stay here.

39:32.036 --> 39:34.121
You tailor your principles to situations.

39:35.039 --> 39:37.458
It's only a slight change in plan.
What's the big deal?

39:38.125 --> 39:41.003
Isn't this what you call flexibility?

39:44.382 --> 39:46.008
We'll do our job.

39:46.634 --> 39:48.969
You do yours and look into Sachimoto.

39:49.804 --> 39:50.805
All right?

39:52.807 --> 39:53.724
Chae-ok.

39:54.225 --> 39:55.142
I'm coming.

40:00.940 --> 40:05.778
Wow, those two sure are quick
to take initiative. Right, Master Jang?

40:14.286 --> 40:15.579
Hey, you there!

40:16.122 --> 40:18.707
This area is off-limits to outsiders.

40:19.208 --> 40:20.042
Who are you?

40:20.126 --> 40:22.545
Oh, apologies!

40:22.628 --> 40:24.713
We were only looking for the restroom.

40:24.797 --> 40:26.215
Let us go, Master.

40:27.383 --> 40:28.592
Wait just a minute!

40:35.766 --> 40:37.643
Oh, there you are.

40:41.522 --> 40:45.651
I checked, and Dr. Takahashi
is indeed out of the office today.

40:46.861 --> 40:48.529
Oh, is that so?

40:48.612 --> 40:50.990
There must have been a misunderstanding.

40:51.866 --> 40:53.200
Dear me…

40:53.284 --> 40:54.535
Is he a visitor?

40:55.744 --> 40:58.831
Yes, he is Dr. Takahashi's outpatient.

41:08.757 --> 41:10.092
You must leave now.

41:12.511 --> 41:13.721
This is an emergency.

41:14.805 --> 41:21.145
All visitors and outpatients
with appointments must leave the premises.

41:21.228 --> 41:23.689
- Why is the military here?
- I repeat.

41:23.772 --> 41:24.690
What is going on?

41:24.773 --> 41:31.363
All visitors and outpatients
with appointments must leave the premises!

41:32.364 --> 41:34.158
Please exit the building, everyone.

41:38.496 --> 41:41.123
Colonel Kato. Please give the order.

41:41.207 --> 41:43.876
The lab door might break any moment now!

41:46.337 --> 41:47.338
Sir!

41:50.925 --> 41:52.301
We're moving it to Level 4.

41:53.594 --> 41:54.762
Prepare the nitrogen.

41:54.845 --> 41:55.888
Yes, sir!

41:55.971 --> 41:57.890
Nitrogen! Bring the nitrogen!

41:57.973 --> 41:58.974
Yes, sir!

42:06.607 --> 42:08.192
There's nothing to worry about.

42:10.277 --> 42:12.988
We are moving you to a place
more fitting of a goddess.

42:14.240 --> 42:15.366
What was that about?

42:17.785 --> 42:19.662
I'm sure they will be fine.

42:19.745 --> 42:21.455
They are supposed to be experts.

42:22.248 --> 42:25.251
Once they confirm Myeong-ja's in there,
they will get out of there.

42:26.585 --> 42:29.255
- About those two…
- Yeah.

42:30.673 --> 42:33.384
They seem to take their work
as seriously as I do, right?

42:57.283 --> 42:59.702
NO ENTRY

43:01.120 --> 43:02.538
NO ENTRY

43:03.956 --> 43:05.457
NO ENTRY

43:36.447 --> 43:37.281
Any movement?

43:38.115 --> 43:40.784
None, sir. It seems to be fully asleep.

44:24.828 --> 44:26.580
What are all these, sir?

44:27.081 --> 44:30.417
They seem to be… some kind of spores.

44:31.085 --> 44:32.169
They're anthrax.

44:33.045 --> 44:36.882
It's protecting itself even in its sleep.

44:37.466 --> 44:39.134
We're done moving it, sir.

44:39.218 --> 44:40.302
Close the door.

44:53.440 --> 44:54.692
Move it to Level 4.

44:54.775 --> 44:57.736
Don't stop injecting nitrogen
during transportation.

44:57.820 --> 44:59.822
Avoid contact with the spores in the air.

44:59.905 --> 45:01.407
Let us all be careful.

45:01.490 --> 45:02.825
Yes, sir!

45:02.908 --> 45:03.742
Start moving!

46:20.778 --> 46:22.112
I guess it's snow.

46:24.114 --> 46:25.491
It melts away quickly.

47:24.633 --> 47:25.634
Help!

48:07.342 --> 48:08.927
Marvelous.

48:36.830 --> 48:39.833
Didn't you say the Japanese soldiers
are being treated here?

48:39.917 --> 48:42.169
Most patients stay
on the second and third floors.

48:42.252 --> 48:45.797
The first floor has offices,
communications rooms, and liaison offices.

48:49.718 --> 48:51.845
More like a military facility
than a hospital.

48:51.929 --> 48:55.515
The security is so tight
that I'm not allowed to go near it.

48:55.599 --> 48:59.102
I only get to go in once every two days
to clean the wards.

48:59.186 --> 49:01.396
Why is that eastern watchtower empty?

49:02.022 --> 49:04.691
A man fell to his death once
because it was too weak.

49:04.775 --> 49:08.570
There were talks of renovation,
but it's been neglected since then.

49:09.655 --> 49:11.239
Can you make it to that tower?

49:16.119 --> 49:17.454
It won't be easy,

49:18.372 --> 49:19.206
but I can do it.

49:19.289 --> 49:20.916
- I'll be back.
- Wait.

49:24.211 --> 49:25.295
Hey…

50:40.912 --> 50:41.913
Where did she go?

51:34.174 --> 51:35.592
- Quickly!
- Yes, sir!

51:43.850 --> 51:46.103
- What should we do, sir?
- Get ready to move!

51:46.186 --> 51:47.187
- Yes, sir!
- Move out!

51:47.270 --> 51:48.355
Move it!

51:49.356 --> 51:50.440
Quickly!

51:50.524 --> 51:52.109
- Hurry!
- Come on!

51:53.110 --> 51:54.653
- Prepare to move.
- Yes, sir!

51:55.445 --> 51:57.280
- To the basement!
- Yes, sir!

51:58.949 --> 52:00.867
Move along! Quickly!

53:00.677 --> 53:02.179
You're still here?

53:07.934 --> 53:09.603
Talk to me. What is it now?

53:11.563 --> 53:13.148
I simply don't understand why.

53:14.399 --> 53:15.483
Why what?

53:16.651 --> 53:18.486
Why it bothers me so much.

53:19.321 --> 53:20.906
What does?

53:27.829 --> 53:29.873
I mean, look at the mess I'm in.

53:30.540 --> 53:33.585
Ishikawa has my life in his hands.

53:34.252 --> 53:38.798
If I don't find Myeong-ja,
my entire fortune will be confiscated,

53:38.882 --> 53:42.385
and I could even be dragged off to war.

53:42.469 --> 53:45.513
Moreover, hyenas and vultures
are circling this shop,

53:45.597 --> 53:48.391
eager to take a bite of whatever they can.

53:50.894 --> 53:52.896
So, why am I so…

53:54.856 --> 53:56.316
bothered by her?

53:56.900 --> 53:58.443
You mean the sleuth girl?

53:59.361 --> 54:00.195
Who?

54:00.278 --> 54:01.988
The "her" you just mentioned.

54:02.072 --> 54:03.073
"Her"?

54:05.492 --> 54:06.743
Did I just say that?

54:06.826 --> 54:08.411
How unfortunate.

54:09.037 --> 54:10.956
They say there's no cure for lovesickness.

54:11.039 --> 54:13.625
Whoa, lovesickness? Watch what you say!

54:13.708 --> 54:15.252
I'm Jang Tae-sang.

54:15.335 --> 54:18.546
All the beautiful girls in this city
couldn't even make me flinch.

54:18.630 --> 54:21.633
Bukchon's hottest guy!
Namchon's number one man!

54:21.716 --> 54:23.468
Which proves that you're lovesick.

54:24.094 --> 54:27.055
You turned your nose up
at all those beauties,

54:28.348 --> 54:29.557
and look at you now.

54:30.267 --> 54:32.686
Of all the girls,
a sleuth girl stole your heart.

54:32.769 --> 54:34.604
No, it's not like that at all!

54:34.688 --> 54:36.147
What is it, then?

54:36.231 --> 54:38.066
You know…

54:40.360 --> 54:42.279
Well… humanism?

54:42.362 --> 54:43.780
Humanism?

54:44.364 --> 54:45.240
Yes, humanism.

54:46.032 --> 54:47.701
Love for mankind.

54:48.785 --> 54:54.040
I'm worrying and pondering
purely out of my love for mankind.

54:54.124 --> 54:54.958
Got that?

54:55.041 --> 54:56.626
Then there's no need to worry.

54:56.710 --> 54:59.004
I should have dragged her out of there.

54:59.587 --> 55:02.757
I shouldn't have left her
at the hospital like that, right?

55:02.841 --> 55:05.010
If you have time to waste,
go find Sachimoto.

55:06.177 --> 55:09.347
Standing there worrying
won't change a single thing.

55:09.431 --> 55:13.143
Be the man that you are
and show us how you do things your way!

55:13.226 --> 55:15.478
Do your part is what I'm saying.

55:20.483 --> 55:21.484
Do you think so?

55:24.446 --> 55:25.280
You're right.

55:26.698 --> 55:28.116
Where are you going?

55:28.199 --> 55:30.702
I'm off to do my part my way.

55:48.094 --> 55:49.220
What gives?

55:51.139 --> 55:54.517
I refuse to drive you around anymore.

55:56.478 --> 55:59.773
Okay. All right. Just write this down.

55:59.856 --> 56:02.817
Sachimoto. A Japanese male in his mid-30s.

56:05.028 --> 56:06.029
Write it down.

56:08.156 --> 56:09.407
A professional painter.

56:09.491 --> 56:12.660
Ask Commissioner Ishikawa
to search for such a man

56:12.744 --> 56:15.330
among the residents of Gyeongseong.

56:15.413 --> 56:19.542
This is crucial to finding Myeong-ja,
so he needs to be thorough, understand?

56:19.626 --> 56:20.710
- Yes.
- Okay!

56:38.144 --> 56:39.145
Enjoy.

56:50.865 --> 56:52.117
Who are you drawing?

56:56.454 --> 56:57.622
My apologies.

56:58.415 --> 57:01.042
The woman in the drawing
looked like she was from Joseon.

57:04.045 --> 57:06.506
How can you tell?

57:08.550 --> 57:09.759
The parting of her hair.

57:13.263 --> 57:14.180
Is that right?

57:16.099 --> 57:18.518
You are very skilled at drawing.

57:19.686 --> 57:21.187
I guess you're a painter?

57:32.740 --> 57:34.117
Breaking news!

57:34.200 --> 57:36.619
Ongseong Hospital
will be closed indefinitely!

57:36.703 --> 57:39.706
Ongseong Hospital closes indefinitely
due to an unknown contagion!

57:39.789 --> 57:41.291
- Choi was right.
- Breaking news!

57:41.374 --> 57:43.668
- This is about yesterday.
- Breaking news!

57:44.669 --> 57:47.422
- It will be closed indefinitely!
- Breaking news!

57:47.505 --> 57:48.923
It's an unknown contagion!

57:49.007 --> 57:52.010
ONGSEONG HOSPITAL CLOSED INDEFINITELY
POSSIBLY DUE TO CONTAGIOUS DISEASE

57:56.931 --> 57:58.141
Get off now!

57:58.975 --> 58:00.685
Hurry! Move your feet!

58:01.519 --> 58:02.437
Faster!

58:02.520 --> 58:03.646
Build the barricades.

58:04.147 --> 58:05.482
I said, hurry up!

58:05.565 --> 58:06.941
Get off! Move them quickly!

58:08.735 --> 58:09.569
CLOSED

58:09.652 --> 58:10.695
Speed it up!

58:31.216 --> 58:34.260
What are you talking about?
The hospital's surrounded by soldiers?

58:34.344 --> 58:38.848
No one can get in from the outside,
and no one can get out from the inside.

58:38.932 --> 58:41.851
They even had machine guns.
It looks pretty serious, sir.

58:43.144 --> 58:44.812
No word from the sleuths yet?

58:45.438 --> 58:47.774
I don't think
they made it out of the hospital.

58:54.447 --> 58:56.866
Master Jang. Where are you going?

58:56.950 --> 58:58.326
Want me to come with you?

58:59.285 --> 59:00.662
Go after him already.

59:00.745 --> 59:02.705
Okay! I was about to!

59:18.054 --> 59:22.267
I checked, and Dr. Takahashi
is indeed out of the office today.

59:22.850 --> 59:24.060
What brings you here?

59:31.901 --> 59:34.487
WE FOUND MYEONG-JA

59:36.322 --> 59:38.074
What about the person
who gave this to you?

59:38.658 --> 59:40.243
They are still inside.

59:41.536 --> 59:43.288
I managed to escape

59:43.371 --> 59:45.707
before the hospital
got completely shut down,

59:47.292 --> 59:48.293
just as dawn broke.

59:49.752 --> 59:52.046
Those people, are they safe?

59:54.090 --> 59:55.174
I don't know.

59:55.258 --> 59:58.970
Is it true that an infectious disease
has spread in there?

01:00:00.763 --> 01:00:01.681
I don't know.

01:00:01.764 --> 01:00:03.600
Please be honest with me!

01:00:04.892 --> 01:00:07.186
What's going on in there right now?

01:00:07.270 --> 01:00:09.147
I don't know either!

01:00:14.611 --> 01:00:16.029
Last night…

01:00:18.448 --> 01:00:20.617
so many people died at the hospital.

01:00:22.660 --> 01:00:25.955
Countless people lost their lives.

01:00:26.539 --> 01:00:28.041
I don't know why.

01:00:28.124 --> 01:00:30.335
And there's no way I can find out.

01:00:33.046 --> 01:00:34.130
Why you?

01:00:35.340 --> 01:00:39.093
Why did you bring this note to me?
Answer me.

01:00:54.817 --> 01:00:58.029
Horrific things are happening
inside Ongseong Hospital right now.

01:00:58.863 --> 01:01:02.075
People are dying like crazy,
but we don't know why.

01:01:03.117 --> 01:01:07.080
My comrades attempted
to find out the truth multiple times…

01:01:09.707 --> 01:01:11.167
but no one made it back.

01:01:14.420 --> 01:01:15.463
This time

01:01:16.464 --> 01:01:17.965
may be no exception.

01:01:21.844 --> 01:01:24.806
WE FOUND MYEONG-JA

01:01:52.291 --> 01:01:54.377
- Mr. Gu.
- Yes, go on.

01:01:55.128 --> 01:01:57.672
I'm afraid I have to go in there myself.

01:01:57.755 --> 01:01:59.006
Go in where?

01:01:59.924 --> 01:02:01.843
- Ongseong Hospital.
- Master Jang!

01:02:01.926 --> 01:02:03.428
- Master.
- Master?

01:02:05.263 --> 01:02:06.389
Get everything ready.

01:02:07.306 --> 01:02:08.766
I'm going in.

01:02:15.398 --> 01:02:16.482
Stuck in my head

01:02:16.566 --> 01:02:18.735
I've been searchin' for the reason

01:02:21.446 --> 01:02:23.239
Nameless longing

01:02:23.322 --> 01:02:25.742
I've been waitin' for you for so long

01:02:27.285 --> 01:02:28.745
But got no direction

01:02:28.828 --> 01:02:31.247
No matter I wanna reach you

01:02:32.165 --> 01:02:33.458
Another way you runnin'

01:02:33.541 --> 01:02:35.042
Goin' on and on

01:02:35.126 --> 01:02:36.919
But need a way to get to you

01:02:39.464 --> 01:02:41.382
You

01:02:41.883 --> 01:02:44.552
You know I'm so stuck with you

01:02:44.635 --> 01:02:45.511
No, oh, oh, oh

01:02:45.595 --> 01:02:47.388
You

01:02:47.930 --> 01:02:50.558
Babe, I don't care at all

01:02:50.641 --> 01:02:53.561
You'll never know what I could do

01:02:53.644 --> 01:02:56.314
You'll never know
What we could have been

01:02:56.397 --> 01:02:59.317
For you
No, oh, oh, oh, oh

01:02:59.400 --> 01:03:01.402
Do you know

01:03:01.486 --> 01:03:02.528
Oh, no

01:03:02.612 --> 01:03:04.071
All the way I found you here

01:03:05.364 --> 01:03:07.325
Oh, I'll be right back for you

01:03:07.408 --> 01:03:08.409
Oh, no

01:03:08.493 --> 01:03:10.161
All the way I found you here

01:03:11.370 --> 01:03:13.331
Oh, I'll be right back for you

01:03:13.414 --> 01:03:14.874
Oh, no

01:03:18.503 --> 01:03:21.756
Chasing the lights
